! Names for the keysyms Ubuntu 24.04's keyboard data uses and its libX11 does not know yet.
!
! xkeyboard-config 2.41 maps Linux key codes to keysyms that xorgproto added after the libX11 in
! the image was built, so xkbcomp cannot resolve them and the X server prints a "Could not resolve
! keysym" warning for each at every start. libX11 reads this file for keysym names it was not
! built with. Values from xorgproto's XF86keysym.h: _EVDEVK(code) = 0x10081000 + code.
!
! Harmless either way: every one of these sits on a key code above 255, which X11's core protocol
! cannot carry, so none of them is ever on the keymap a Bot's browser types through.
XF86CameraAccessEnable	:1008124B
XF86CameraAccessDisable	:1008124C
XF86CameraAccessToggle	:1008124D
XF86NextElement	:1008127B
XF86PreviousElement	:1008127C
XF86AutopilotEngageToggle	:1008127D
XF86MarkWaypoint	:1008127E
XF86Sos	:1008127F
XF86NavChart	:10081280
XF86FishingChart	:10081281
XF86SingleRangeRadar	:10081282
XF86DualRangeRadar	:10081283
XF86RadarOverlay	:10081284
XF86TraditionalSonar	:10081285
XF86ClearvuSonar	:10081286
XF86SidevuSonar	:10081287
XF86NavInfo	:10081288
